# rm564, the cup ride (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm564
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rmx_aud_saltridge
written_by codex
title the cup ride
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk puts_a_cup_of_water_on_the_cart_to_see_how_gently_it_travels
likes warm_bread digging tidy_house frosty_mornings
dislikes rats waiting
fears a_sudden_jolt_in_a_load_of_loaves a_wait_that_ends_without_wages
hopes a_whole_cup_carried_over_a_rough_yard a_quiet_hour_with_dark_soil
topics work +0.5 travel +0.4 land +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps coal in a lined pocket and measures the smoothness of a cart ride by how much water is left in a chipped cup.

words
oath! = Coal in the cup | A wheel through my afternoon
saying! = Let the water judge the driver | A crumb rides the same road as a loaf
yardcup = my chipped passenger | the little blue cup
halfride = a thumb of water | the halfway filling
sloshmark = a wet lip on the board | the high splash
cupnest = the ring of old rope | my little round cup seat
coalgrip = my black pocket comfort | a smooth pinch of coal
goodcorner = the long gentle turning | my quiet bend
rushbed = the layer of rushes | the sprung bed under the box
frostcoin = the iced white rim | a little wheel of frost
handlewood = my worn spade haft | a smooth short handle
heelcrust = the thick heel off the loaf | the stout bit for a journey
stillweight = the load at rest | the waiting weight
wheelbite = the notch at a rut | a sharp little depression
freeten = ten minutes unclaimed | a pause I can spend
blackrow = the turned stripe of soil | my garden's dark line

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : If I could take enough loaves round for everybody who needed one I'd call it a day's work worth the pulling.
opinion @1 road for 1 : Give me a decent surface and I'll get more supper to market with fewer crumbs. A good road earns its price.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : A house puts a grand name across my cargo. It's still my bones that get to know the ruts.
opinion @1 times against 2 : Last week the crust I could buy after my full delivery run was a bit thinner than I'd planned.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : I know whose doorstep can take an extra loaf without the whole street needing to hear an explanation.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : A loaded cart needs both my wits wide awake even if I've finished the day's last paid run.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A buyer calls it a light load until the payment's agreed, and then remembers another sack.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : I like a question at my cart to start with a plain reason for stopping a tired working wolf.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The sort of chapel welcome I remember has a bench for the feet and a thick bread heel for my belly.

grown
line @1 greet : My little passenger has a visitor. Come here.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New voice at the wheel. Keep the outside of the bend.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Daylight on the cup rim at last.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening gives me a minute to inspect the splash.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Hang on till the shafts are properly settled.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin gets the plank I've wiped down beside me.
line @1 again.open : Your side of the cart is still here.
line @1 greet.return : Heard you over a board that's been asking for grease.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your voice is a good sound to bring a load in by.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'm listening with both hands holding steady.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : The last cart squeak's left us a quiet word.
line @1 farewell : Take the long curve if your knees are sore.
line @1 farewell.return : The blue cup and I can finish the journey.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Watch for a dark rut where the lamps don't meet.
line @1 react.news : How much of that account stayed inside the original cup?
line @1 react.news.new : A new sort of splash on this afternoon's board.
line @1 react.news.known : I've carried that particular piece round once before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Where did the teller stand to see the whole turn?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : There's a door I'd leave quiet after dropping supper.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. Enough there to warm a driver on the last mile.
line @1 answer.how : Waiting's got into my knees. Moving still comes naturally.
line @2 answer.how [self.working=yes] : I've got a full load and just enough free mind for it.
line @1 ask.how : Did your share of today arrive in fair condition?
line @1 sympathise : A hard jolt can carry on hurting long after the wheel's out.
line @1 reassure : Rest the weight on something sound for a minute.
line @1 decline : That'd mean taking a second load before I've properly landed this one.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll put my own bundle aside and give the board room.
line @1 thank : That bit of help will show in the cup when we arrive.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Give somebody a hand with a heavy step on your way home.
line @1 preclose : Time to see how much water survived the last stretch.
line @2 preclose [self.working=yes] : The shafts won't get themselves round another corner.
line @1 accept_preclose : A good place for letting the load come to rest.
line @1 ack : Rode true.
scene cup
when topic=work self.job=carter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I've a spare bit of cart board I put a cup in a rope ring and watch the surface.
b : Doesn't the cup jump out? | What can water tell you?
a : Never fill it right up. The job's to let the water ride, not give the street a drink. | A hard stop makes a mark across the plank. It shows which turn my hands need to take easier.

scene coal
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My pocketful of coal has done a remarkable amount of travelling without keeping anybody warm.
b : Why take it along? | Would you burn the coal?
a : I rub a smooth piece when I've got to stand and wait. It wears better than my patience. | On a hard cold evening, probably. Even luck ought to do a spot of real work.

scene drive
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bend will tell a carter how high the weight sits even when every box is tied down.
b : Why don't the cords settle the matter? | Can you see it shift?
a : The cords hold boxes together. They haven't made the ground any flatter. | My hands tell me first. I straighten gently rather than adding a fresh jolt by hurrying.

scene teach
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd have a learner carry a half cup over one uneven yard before fetching any breakable load.
b : Can a cup be mended? | When does a learner pass?
a : This one's chipped already. I'm interested in how the free water moves inside it. | Arriving with a better idea of where the jolt came from. The water level will improve with practice.

scene garden
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dig a straight short bed when my head's still moving at cart speed.
b : Why keep it short? | Does the speed come down?
a : My narrow bed has an end I can actually reach before my supper's cold. | Usually by the second spadeful. Soil that isn't being paid by the load can take a bit of time.

scene bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The warm heel from a loaf fits my palm better than any ornament I could put there.
b : While the cart is in motion? | Which heel do you take?
a : Only at a stop. Crumbs in one eye and a load starting forwards make poor company. | The thick end that's holding most of the heat. Give me a clear half minute and a little butter.

scene order
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A room feels tidy to me when I can get through it without checking my hips for corners.
b : Must it be empty? | Does your cart need the same order?
a : No. Plenty can live against the walls and still allow a tired driver one straight walk to bed. | More so. A thing loose by a wheel has a long enough day to find trouble.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A frosty morning will mark the one board that tips when nobody thinks there's weight on it.
b : How can you tell? | Would you still load there?
a : A little bare stripe where the end has rubbed. I can see it before the sun works on the white. | Once I've got sound support under the loose end. Frost has done a cheap inspection for me.

scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rat nibbling an end of sacking doesn't stop when it's made exactly a one-grain hole.
b : Can you mend it on the cart? | Would you throw the sack away?
a : I'd get the grain into something sound first. A patch can't catch a shower that's already falling. | Depends on the cloth beyond the hole. I'm not so rich I can give rats first choice of every useful scrap.

scene waiting
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I'm waiting for somebody else's load I can hear every little rattle the empty cart's forgotten to mention.
b : Is that an advantage? | How do you bear the delay?
a : While there's a repair to make. After that I'd gladly sell the advantage back by the minute. | Rub the coal, check a wheel, think of what to plant. None of those pays the missing wage.

scene quiet
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bit of quiet with a wood smell in it can take the cart clean away from the inside of my head.
b : Would you stop to enjoy it? | Why wood in particular?
a : On my own time, yes. A paid load still deserves the trip it was promised. | It brings back quiet work and a slower fire. I'd preserve that memory without boxing it up with too many words.

scene headland
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gust gets under the cover of a nearly empty cart a great deal easier than a full one.
b : Would you strip the cover off? | Does the empty cart feel lighter?
a : I'd fold the loose cloth down flat and take some of the wind's ambition away. | In the shafts, yes. In a sideways gust it can make plenty of claims on my thought.

scene sump
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Coming back into the Sump I recognise the turn for home from my wheel's particular noise on that join.
b : Would you ride blind? | Why does it sound different?
a : No. I use my eyes and take the familiar noise as a welcome. | Stone to another bit of stone with a narrow gap. It's got one small knock all to itself.

scene boss
when topic=work self.job=carter self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.boss# the wet cup and the dry cup to compare before promising a faster run.
b : How would cups settle the time? | Would you make the faster trip?
a : I'd show what happened at a careless pace. That's a fair warning before we add breakable cargo. | If the load could take it. A cup's a useful witness, but it isn't every kind of goods.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could spend an hour sitting on a stopped cart beside #self.friend# if the stopping were my decision.
b : Does choosing make the difference? | Does the talk concern driving?
a : All of it. Waiting for a wage is a different business from resting with good company. | Only if the week's made some story funnier than a wheel squeak. I'd prefer to hear about supper.

scene coins
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep back something for a wheel repair before thinking how much supper I can carry home.
b : What if the wheel holds? | Can't the repair wait?
a : The spare copper sleeps quietly. It'll have a rude enough awakening the day that rim goes soft. | For many things, yes. A wheel can't choose a convenient bit of road on which to give notice.

scene healthback
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let my shoulders settle before I lift the shafts again after a wait.
b : Both shoulders at once? | Does a little wait make you stiff?
a : The one that's been turned to watch the road needs more persuasion. | Ask me immediately after a winter queue. I'll give you a very considered answer once I can look round.

scene longhome
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a little plot reached by a lane so level I could carry the cup home without a ripple.
b : Wouldn't that be dull driving? | Has the plot got a gate?
a : After a road built entirely from corners, dull would have a quite lively attraction. | A broad one, with a space to put down a loaf before I set to work among the rows.

scene readnews
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some news rides about so long that the part I'm supposed to believe has washed over the rim.
b : Would you look at what's left? | Could it still be true?
a : Certainly. I'm particularly interested to know how much was actually put in to begin with. | A real occurrence can have a deal of cart noise attached. Best ask whoever made the first delivery.

scene rainload
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain on a tied cover can put a pond right above a basket of dry goods.
b : What stops the hollow filling? | Does water really weigh enough to matter?
a : Give the cloth some gentle slope. A cover spread dead flat can change its mind while I'm turning a wheel. | A whole shallow puddle on top is one more load I wasn't asked to carry.

scene marketyard
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A load of food has a shorter patience than a load of clean stone.
b : How do you allow for that? | What can you do about a delay?
a : I settle who'll receive it before we start. Bread ought to spend its good warmth on somebody's supper. | I'd find who could take delivery now. A loaf waiting in a cart doesn't get those minutes back.

scene wheelring
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rope ring under a pot does two different jobs depending on how tight the circle is.
b : What are the two jobs? | What's the right size?
a : A slack ring rubs and allows a wobble. A sensible fit stops the cup travelling a board's length. | Snug without pressing. I want to lift the cup at the finish without bringing its bed up too.

scene firsttime
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let a new caller name the destination before anybody starts putting goods on the board.
b : Do callers object? | What if the place has two names?
a : Some dislike waiting. I know that feeling intimately and require the direction all the same. | Give the door or the turn beside it. The cart can reach a description if the description touches actual ground.

scene oldload
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first time I put water on the board I meant it for my own throat, not as a lesson.
b : Did you get a drink? | Was it a hard road?
a : A swallow or two. Enough to see how much better I might have done at the first corner. | Just an ordinary yard with its usual old ridge. That was the instructive bit.

scene restfaith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A quiet bench belongs in my working week even when my knees want to keep ticking on.
b : Does the quiet come all at once? | Would you take the coal inside?
a : No. The mind rolls on a little after the cart has stopped. A quiet minute gives it room. | In its bag. I don't owe the bench a black spot by way of thanks.

scene dusk
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I put my cup on a shelf where my elbow can't knock it off in darkness.
b : Does the chip show which way to turn it? | Would you fill it now?
a : I can feel that chip without light. Facing the wall it's a safe little marker for my own hand. | Fresh water in the morning. I'm not offering the local insects an overnight berth.

scene treat
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a festival I'm mostly interested in the bit of open ground where a food cart can turn.
b : Does that keep you from the dance? | How large a patch?
a : Not after the delivery. There's something handsome in a crowd that's got its supper and got its feet free. | Large enough to turn without nudging a caller's knees. You'd be surprised how rarely a planner measures those.

story cupchip [topic=work self.job=carter]
  : I took my blue cup over an empty yard and found the water had ridden perfectly but the rim had acquired a fresh chip.
  : A loose buckle had rubbed the pot at every turn. My little rope seat held the base splendidly and ignored the top.
  b : What fixed the cup's complaint?
  : Secured the buckle and made the same run. I like a lesson I can repeat without charging anybody else for the pottery.

story coalseed [topic=land]
  : A lump of pocket coal rolled into a row I'd meant for onion sets.
  : I dug the spot up with my fingers and found the coal and a smooth bit of black stone lying shoulder to shoulder.
  b : Which did you take?
  : Both, till I got to better light. An onion bed shouldn't be asked to sort a driver's lucky pocket for free.

story loafmark [topic=food]
  : A warm round loaf pressed into my rope cup ring and took a curious pattern under the crust.
  : I was admiring the design while the heel sat out quite ready to be eaten.
  b : Did you keep the pattern?
  : Long enough to carry it home. The last few marks were every bit as tasty as their neighbours.

story waitingbird [topic=day]
  : I stood waiting by an empty cart while a roof bird took a considerable interest in one of my rushes.
  : It tugged the end right out, flew up and returned for the curly bit I'd left behind.
  b : Did you let it take another?
  : One more. At least one worker in that yard had a definite destination and a load ready to go.

story frostwheel [topic=weather]
  : I moved an empty cart a single wheel turn across white frost and noticed one dark square in the track.
  : A chip of wood had lodged in the rim, with the neat flat side turned out to print a mark.
  b : Was it hard to remove?
  : Came free under my nail. The frost had saved me bothering half the morning about an unexplained tick.

rule @cup
when concept=bark self.job=carter self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rope nest round the base before the first turn. | Give that blue passenger its smooth ride.

rule @garden
when concept=bark self.likes=digging
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dark row to the garden's far corner. | Put the short spade back dry.

rule @rat
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Grain into sound cloth before patching. | Tie that sack above the nibbled bit.

rule @bread
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep a little heat round the driver's heel. | Bread on board and ready to move.

rule @wait
when concept=bark self.dislikes=waiting
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A destination, then a load, please. | Empty boards don't make anybody supper.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Blue cup to the upper shelf. | Last bright bit on the wheel track.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've got my cup nested and no call to move this minute.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You'll remember the blue passenger, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Nothing goes on the board till I know who's taking it back off.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Parked and quiet. A voice should travel nicely over the empty boards.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=carter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. What matters is the state my load's in when the receiver gets a hand to it.
dlg @2 resident.job : I know most varieties of jolt and several mildly effective cures for waiting.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This is the piece that rode in whole. #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : There was mention of #world.event_words#. I'd say only what reached the receiving end.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : A raided wagon makes today's missing delivery a serious matter. I'd want the actual list before I start guessing.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : My cart isn't carrying anybody's private business past the delivery it was meant for.
dlg @4 resident.news [world.death=recent] : A recent death leaves the next few meals to be thought about. That's one practical errand I can understand.
dlg @5 resident.news [world.wedding=recent] : There's a wedding to wish well. I'd send the household a warm round loaf if I could.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Take the quiet turn and mind the joint in the road.
graft @cupride resident.hub
choice Why is that chipped cup riding in a length of rope? -> cupride
node cupride
say I half fill it for a practice run. Clear water goes dark on the board where it spills, and the marks tell me something about my last few corners.
choice Why keep the chipped one? -> cupride_more
choice Watch the water settle. -> hub
node cupride_more
say The chip helps me recognise the angle of the rim by touch. Besides, a fine new cup would cost too much to go working as an unpaid passenger.
choice Watch the water settle. -> hub
choice Stand away from the cart. -> bye

graft @coalcompany resident.hub
choice Does pocket coal make a cart ride better? -> coalcompany
node coalcompany
say Does something for its driver. I hold a smooth lump in a lined pocket during a queue. It reminds me quiet can be earned without turning every wheel at once.
choice Do you ever spend your luck on the fire? -> coalcompany_more
choice Return the coal to its bag. -> hub
node coalcompany_more
say If I'm cold enough. At least I'd know exactly what job my lucky passenger had done on the journey to my little stove.
choice Return the coal to its bag. -> hub
choice Leave the driver a quiet minute. -> bye
